    <string name="settings_terms_title">Terms of Service</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">DocuOrg Privacy Policy\n\nLast updated: May 27, 2026\n\nOverview\nWe collect the minimum information needed to provide the service and improve the app.\n\nInformation We Collect\n- Account details you provide (such as email).\n- Documents and metadata you upload or create (title, category, tags, notes).\n- Usage data and crash diagnostics to improve reliability.\n\nHow We Use Information\n- To store, sync, and organize your documents.\n- To deliver requested features like AI extraction and search.\n- To improve performance and fix bugs.\n\nSharing\nWe do not sell your data. We only share with service providers needed to run the app (for example, cloud storage and analytics), under confidentiality obligations.\n\nSecurity\nWe apply reasonable security measures to protect your data, but no system is 100% secure.\n\nYour Choices\nYou can edit or delete documents in the app and sign out at any time.\n\nContact\nQuestions about this policy? Email support@docuorg.app.</string>
    <string name="terms_of_service_body">DocuOrg Terms of Service\n\nLast updated: May 27, 2026\n\nAcceptance of Terms\nBy using DocuOrg, you agree to these terms.\n\nUse of the App\n- Use the app only for lawful purposes.\n- You are responsible for the content you upload.\n\nAccounts\n- Keep your login credentials secure.\n- You are responsible for activity under your account.\n\nContent Ownership\n- You keep ownership of your documents.\n- You grant DocuOrg permission to store and process your content to provide the service.\n\nService Availability\nWe strive for high availability, but the app may be unavailable at times due to maintenance or outages.\n\nLimitations of Liability\nDocuOrg is provided "as is" without warranties. We are not liable for indirect or incidental damages.\n\nChanges\nWe may update these terms. Continued use of the app means you accept the updated terms.\n\nContact\nQuestions about these terms? Email support@docuorg.app.</string>
